    <!-- 1. Curtain cloth: pinned only at 2 corners so it drapes and sways when the robot pushes through. -->
    <!-- Note for later: even at these settings (unchanged from the original authoring), one -->
    <!-- edge of the settled drape sits stretched to ~9x its rest spacing (0.04m) and stays -->
    <!-- there -- <elasticity young=...> has never actually been active (MuJoCo's shell plugin -->
    <!-- isn't registered in this build) and dim=2 flexes can't use edge stiffness (restricted -->
    <!-- to dim=1), so damping is the only real lever here, and it only opposes velocity, not -->
    <!-- that resting stretch. If the sheet ever reads as torn, that steady-state overstretch -->
    <!-- is the actual thing to fix (e.g. more pins, or a finer/differently-proportioned grid), -->
    <!-- not mass or damping -- both were tried and lowering either just destabilizes the sim -->
    <!-- without touching this. -->
